flowchart TB
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: to follow one purchase from the budget line to the bank payment and the audit, which number connects each record to the next one, and where is there no such number?
  %% READING: each box is one record. Line 1 = its name. Line 2 = its own number (this identifies ONE record). Line 3 = the UACS segments it contains (these identify a CLASS of records). The text on each arrow is the key that connects two records. Green arrow = a number or code is copied from one record to the next. Red dotted arrow = no coded key: the link exists only as text, as an attachment, or in a person's knowledge.
  %% SOURCES: UACS segments [JC2017-1]. Column "Code (PAP)" in the procurement plan [APP-FORM]. Fields of the obligation request: responsibility center, particulars, program code, object code, amount [ORS-FORM]. Fields of the LDDAP-ADA: creditor, bank account, ORS number, allotment class per UACS, amounts, fund cluster, MDS sub-account, NCA number [LDDAP-FORM]. Obligations in registries, not in the journal [GAM-GUIDE]. No single system follows a proposal from plan to budget [ROADMAP2024]. In BTMS the voucher is linked to an approved obligation request, and the obligation request can be created from an approved purchase order [BTMS-SITE]. Inconsistent classification codes across PFM systems reported as a gap [SFA6].
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: the fields of the disbursement voucher, of the journal entry voucher and of audit notices (from the forms of the Government Accounting Manual, Volume II, which I did not open), the PhilGEPS reference number, contract and property numbers. Please check these against the actual forms of one agency.

  PIP["Investment program entry<br/>own number: project entry in PIPOL<br/>codes: none from UACS until it enters the budget"]
  BP["Budget proposal line<br/>own number: none (a line in a form in OSBPS)<br/>codes: organization, program code, object or expense class"]
  GAA["GAA line<br/>own number: none (identified by its full code and year)<br/>codes: funding source, organization, program code, expense class"]:::uacs
  ALL["Allotment<br/>own number: SARO number (none when the GAA itself is the allotment order)<br/>codes: funding source, organization, program code, expense class"]:::uacs
  APP["Procurement plan line<br/>own number: line in the Annual Procurement Plan<br/>codes: program code (PAP)"]
  PROC["Procurement<br/>own number: PhilGEPS reference number<br/>codes: none"]
  CON["Contract or purchase order<br/>own number: contract or purchase order number<br/>codes: none"]
  ORS["Obligation<br/>own number: ORS number<br/>codes: responsibility center, program code, object code"]:::uacs
  IAR["Accepted delivery<br/>own number: number of the inspection and acceptance report<br/>codes: none"]
  DV["Approved claim<br/>own number: disbursement voucher number<br/>codes: object (account) code in the accounting entry"]:::uacs
  JEV["Journal entry<br/>own number: JEV number<br/>codes: fund cluster, account codes"]:::uacs
  NCA["Cash authority<br/>own number: NCA number<br/>codes: fund cluster, organization"]:::uacs
  ADA["Payment order<br/>own number: LDDAP-ADA number (or check number)<br/>codes: fund cluster, allotment class"]:::uacs
  BANK["Bank transaction<br/>own number: bank reference<br/>codes: none"]
  ASSET["Asset record<br/>own number: property number<br/>codes: asset account code"]
  REP["Report row (FAR 1 and others)<br/>own number: none (a total per code and period)<br/>codes: fund cluster, organization, program code, expense class or object"]:::uacs
  AUD["Audit finding<br/>own number: number of the observation or notice<br/>codes: none"]

  PIP -. "no common key<br/>(separate systems)" .-> BP
  BP -- "same codes" --> GAA
  GAA -- "same codes" --> ALL
  GAA -- "program code" --> APP
  APP -- "plan line" --> PROC
  PROC -- "PhilGEPS<br/>reference number" --> CON
  ALL -- "same codes" --> ORS
  CON -. "named only in the text<br/>of the ORS (particulars)" .-> ORS
  CON -- "contract number" --> IAR
  ORS -- "ORS number" --> DV
  DV -- "voucher number" --> AUD
  IAR -. "attachment<br/>(paper)" .-> DV
  DV -- "voucher number" --> JEV
  DV -- "ORS number, payee" --> ADA
  NCA -- "NCA number" --> ADA
  ADA -- "LDDAP-ADA or<br/>check number" --> BANK
  IAR -. "by documents" .-> ASSET
  ORS -- "codes" --> REP
  ADA -- "amount paid, by code" --> REP

  linkStyle 0,7,11,16 stroke:#b00020,stroke-width:2px,stroke-dasharray: 4 3
  linkStyle 1,2,3,4,5,6,8,9,10,12,13,14,15,17,18 stroke:#2e6b2e,stroke-width:2px

  N["WHAT THE CHAIN SHOWS: UACS connects the records at the top (budget line, allotment, procurement plan, obligation, report). From the obligation onward the connection is a document number.<br/>The bank transaction contains no program code. Four links have no coded key at all. In agencies that use BTMS, the purchase order, obligation request, voucher and journal entry are created one from the other, so these links are stored by the system."]
  AUD ~~~ N

